Platform detection checks (`isIOS`, `isWeb`) are being used within the component to control behavior, which increases maintenance overhead and complexity.

**Suggested fix:** Create platform-specific file extensions to separate platform concerns:

```tsx
// FormHelpMessage.ios.tsx - iOS-specific implementation
useEffect(() => {
    if (\!shouldAnnounceError || typeof message \!== 'string' || \!message.trim()) {
        return;
    }
    if (previousAnnouncedMessageRef.current === message) {
        return;
    }
    previousAnnouncedMessageRef.current = message;
    AccessibilityInfo.announceForAccessibility(message);
}, [message, shouldAnnounceError]);

// FormHelpMessage.tsx - Base/Web implementation (no AccessibilityInfo call)
```

Alternatively, extract platform-specific logic into a custom hook (e.g., `useAccessibilityAnnouncement`) that has platform-specific implementations.

