While this PR correctly adds `sanitizeSearchValue()` for the `limit` value (fixing the space-handling bug), there is an inconsistency in the same function: lines 628-629 handle `sortBy` and `sortOrder` without using `sanitizeSearchValue()`.

**Current inconsistency:**
```ts
// Lines 628-629 - NOT sanitized
filtersString.push(`${CONST.SEARCH.SYNTAX_ROOT_KEYS.SORT_BY}:${options?.sortBy ?? CONST.SEARCH.TABLE_COLUMNS.DATE}`);
filtersString.push(`${CONST.SEARCH.SYNTAX_ROOT_KEYS.SORT_ORDER}:${options?.sortOrder ?? CONST.SEARCH.SORT_ORDER.DESC}`);

// Lines 632-659 - ARE sanitized
const sanitizedType = sanitizeSearchValue(type);
const sanitizedGroupBy = sanitizeSearchValue(groupBy);
const sanitizedView = sanitizeSearchValue(view);
const sanitizedStatus = sanitizeSearchValue(status);
// ... columns also sanitized

// Line 785 - NOW sanitized (this PR)
filtersString.push(`${CONST.SEARCH.SYNTAX_ROOT_KEYS.LIMIT}:${sanitizeSearchValue(limitValue.toString())}`);
```

**Recommendation:**
For consistency and to prevent similar bugs, consider wrapping `sortBy` and `sortOrder` values with `sanitizeSearchValue()` as well:
```ts
filtersString.push(`${CONST.SEARCH.SYNTAX_ROOT_KEYS.SORT_BY}:${sanitizeSearchValue(options?.sortBy ?? CONST.SEARCH.TABLE_COLUMNS.DATE)}`);
filtersString.push(`${CONST.SEARCH.SYNTAX_ROOT_KEYS.SORT_ORDER}:${sanitizeSearchValue(options?.sortOrder ?? CONST.SEARCH.SORT_ORDER.DESC)}`);
```

